diff --git a/docs/GBA.md b/docs/GBA.md
index a481542..f53e097 100644
--- a/docs/GBA.md
+++ b/docs/GBA.md
@@ -2946,7 +2946,13 @@ laid out, a stamp or picture is asked for the first time); the fog's work maximu
 **Costs.** ROM +4.24 MB: `backdrops.bin` 3,659,772 -> 7,897,220 B (family 4, 99 pictures, 1.98 MB: the 82 cloud pictures 1.57 MB, 10 Vapula
 poses 384 KB, the room, the fog, two skies, two bands; family 5, 261 stamps, 2.25 MB) and `.text` +1,440 B. EWRAM, IWRAM resident, the overlay groups: 0 B
 (`make -C gba sizes`: `.bss` 254,828 B, `.iwram` 11,272 B, `.iwram_bss` 4,088 B, the four overlay groups, the same as the base).
-PS1: the new code is `#if !defined(DOOMO_PLATFORM_PS1)`; the three functions that serve both (`puff_draw`, the cloud, the demon) are the old code.
+PS1: the kept code is `#if !defined(DOOMO_PLATFORM_PS1)` and the four vignettes' draw functions keep their old text for the PS1 (a first cut that
+shared them grew the PS1 object by 840 B). Measured on `fe41002` (base) and base + S3-7, both built with the boot FMV: `_end` 0x801e0420 and the
+margin 130,000 B below the stack top in both (the image is the same but for 3 bytes of the overlay table: the story group is 16 B bigger, `cutscene.c`'s
+text 29,408 -> 29,424 B, and OVL.BIN is the same size, the slot unchanged), so **resident delta 0 B**; `game_smoke` passes; `speed2.sh cutscene` (16
+windows) gives the same numbers and 16 of 16 byte-identical shots on both discs. The PS1 windows for the later shots, which the audit did not measure, do
+**not** hold 30 on either disc (same code): eruption shot 2 / 3 / 4 29.4 / 23.0 / 19.2 fps (the big cloud's circles), Vapula shot 3 27.0 fps. The
+owner's trade-offs are GBA-only; a PS1 / Dreamcast fix for those windows is a separate package.
 
 ## 4b. Retained panels (G7, `src/panel.c`)
 
