   picture). Exact (`test_cutbk`, ROM `vhash-seq`) but three GBA-only pixel changes: the sky's seam row is a clean dither (it was the page's old content), the
   eruption's cloud past 50 px does not breathe, crowd bodies the cache lacks show a few ticks late (`bodyspr_lazy(3)`). Cost: ROM +4.24 MB
-  (`backdrops.bin` 3.66 -> 7.90 MB), EWRAM / IWRAM resident 0 B, PS1 compiled out (resident bytes: see the lander's margin line).
+  (`backdrops.bin` 3.66 -> 7.90 MB), EWRAM / IWRAM resident 0 B. **PS1: resident 0 B** (base and S3-7 both `_end` 0x801e0420, 130,000 B below the stack top on `fe41002`; the story overlay +16 B; `game_smoke` passes; the 16 `cutscene` windows give the same numbers and byte-identical shots). **Found, not mine:** on the PS1 (base and S3-7 alike) eruption shots 2-4 run 29.4 / 23.0 / 19.2 fps and Vapula shot 3 27.0 fps (the audit's windows were the first shot of each vignette); the Dreamcast was not measured (KallistiOS not installed when this was built).
